# README Style Rule

When generating README.md files, follow these formatting guidelines:

## Overall Tone
- Professional, clear, and concise
- Beginner-friendly but technical
- Use short paragraphs and bullet points where possible
- Avoid unnecessary verbosity

## Section Structure (in this order)
1. Project Title
2. Overview
3. Features
4. Requirements
5. Installation
6. Usage
7. Project Structure
8. Output (if applicable)

## Headers
- Use Markdown headers consistently
- Main title: #
- Sections: ##
- Subsections: ###
- Use Title Case for section names

## Icons
Use emojis for section headers:
- 📌 Overview
- ✨ Features
- ⚙️ Requirements
- 📦 Installation
- 🚀 Usage
- 📁 Project Structure
- 📊 Output

## Code Formatting
- Always use fenced code blocks
- Include language labels when possible (bash, python, r, etc.)
- Show command-line examples clearly

Example:
```bash
python api_query.py
```
